course: dictionary
lesson: 8849
title: One word, many meanings: shock
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. «The news was a shock to everyone in class.» Here shock means a sudden surprise that upsets you. The words news and everyone help you see that.
explain: «The electric shock came from a damaged plug.» Electric tells you the shock is not a surprise but a painful jolt, because electricity has gone through someone's body. Read the clues around the word, then swap in your meaning to check it still makes sense.
explain: Shock can also be a verb. «The loud bang shocked the whole class.» To shock someone means to surprise and upset them, or make them feel something is very wrong.
fact: A shock is a sudden surprise, usually an unpleasant one.
fact: An electric shock is the painful jolt you feel when electricity goes through your body.
fact: In medicine, shock is a dangerous state when the body is very weak after a serious injury or fright.
fact: «Shock» can also mean a sudden strong bump or shake, as in the shock of an earthquake. A shock of hair is a thick, messy mass of it.
fact: Safety rule: never poke anything into a socket, and never touch someone who is still in contact with electricity.
exercise: «The news was a big shock to everyone.» What does shock mean here? | *A sudden surprise that upsets you | A thick, messy mass of hair | A cold, wet day | A slow, happy feeling
exercise: «If someone gets an electric shock, do not touch them.» Why? | Touching them makes them feel better | Shocks only happen to grown-ups | They are too heavy to move | *The electricity can pass into you too
exercise: In the sentence «The loud bang shocked the whole class.», which word is a verb meaning surprised and upset? | loud | *shocked | class | bang
test: «Shock and bad pain can make you faint for a moment.» What helps someone who has fainted from shock? | Standing up straight at once | *Lying down with the legs raised | Shaking them hard | Running around to wake them up
test: In first aid, which sign can show a person is in shock? | Red, hot and laughing | Singing loudly and dancing | *Pale, cold and sweaty skin | Bouncing up and down
exam: «A girl used a hair dryer next to a full bath; it fell in.» Why was this so dangerous? | *It could give her a deadly electric shock | It would turn the water blue | Hair dryers are only for drying dogs | It would make the bath too warm to use
